        <briefdescription>
<para>Return the plugin internal representation of a module execution config. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This is a tuple with a module name (mandatory), a method name for the execution to start with (defaults to &quot;run&quot;), and a list of arguments to pass to the launcher that performs the execution. The arguments, as per Gradle convention, should be possible to be configured lazily as a provider, so they can be calculated at the time of execution, and not at the time of configuration. </para>
<para>TODO: This is not supported everywhere yet, but please feel free to add DSL logic for that, where you find it missing, and unit tests to make sure it works.</para>
